<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Xianzhong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1606">1606</a>–1647</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Xianzhong was a peasant rebel leader of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>. After years of campaigning across northern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a> in 1644 and proclaimed the Great Xi state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a>. His rule is notorious for mass killings that devastated the province's population, and he was killed by Qing forces in 1647.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhang-xianzhong.jpg" alt="Zhang Xianzhong" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: （清）松排山人（編）；《古本小說集成》編委會 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BC%B5%E7%8D%BB%E5%BF%A0.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
